{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.FaddeevRatioPeriodic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DoublyPeriodicLiouville"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.ratio_const_of_entire","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.ratio_const_of_entire","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L69-L76","doc":"The entire instance recovers the reduction: an entire ratio of two solutions is constant,\nwith **both** periods derived (compare `FaddeevRigidityReduction.uniqueUpToScalar_of_entire`,\nwhich takes the `i/b`-period as a hypothesis and needs `Φ` nowhere zero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.entireClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.entireClass","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L62-L67","doc":"**The holomorphic instance** (Liouville): entire functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.ratio_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.ratio_const","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L42-L60","doc":"**Faddeev–Volkov rigidity in any compact-curve class.**  If the ratio of two `FaddeevPhi`\nsolutions lies in the class, it is constant. Both periods of the ratio are derived from the\nshift equations plus continuity (`periodic_b_of_continuous`, `periodic_binv_of_continuous`);\nno nowhere-zero hypothesis and no separate `i/b`-periodicity input is needed. The only\nanalytic content is the class's own axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.const_of_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.const_of_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.continuous_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.continuous_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.mem","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevCompactCurve.CompactCurveClass","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevCompactCurve.lean#L33-L40","doc":"**A function class with the compact-curve axiom** for the lattice spanned by `bas`:\nits members are continuous, and a member periodic under the lattice is constant — the\nstatement `H⁰(E, O) = ℂ` for `E = ℂ / (ℤ·bas 0 + ℤ·bas 1)`. This is the elliptic analogue of\nthe `H⁰(ℙ¹, O(−1)) = 0` axiom of the Bloch–Wigner rigidity class (PR #7946). ","signatureChunk":0}]}